Package: kolinos-desktop
Architecture: @KOLIN_DEB_ARCH@
Maintainer: KolinOS <dev@kolinos.org>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Depends: kolinos-theme, kolinos-tools,
 openbox, picom, tint2, xterm, feh, rofi, xinit, x11-xserver-utils,
 libgl1-mesa-dri, adwaita-icon-theme, fonts-inter, fonts-jetbrains-mono
Recommends: pcmanfm, gtk2-engines-murrine
Suggests: lightdm, lightdm-gtk-greeter
Description: KolinOS "Corvo Glass" lightweight desktop
 Metapackage that pulls in the KolinOS graphical session: the openbox window
 manager, the picom compositor (which produces the frosted-glass look), the
 tint2 panel, a terminal, the rofi launcher and the Corvo Glass theme.
 .
 It is deliberately light (X11, no full desktop environment) so it can run on
 phones and other low-RAM ARM64 devices. Starting the session requires an X
 server: on real hardware an Xorg server or lightdm; under Termux the
 Termux:X11 app. This package installs the desktop, it does not provide a
 display server on its own.
